eam of multi-faceted women who are proud to bring you feeding advice to help make your life easier. Learn more about us and our work with BLW Meals and Kids Meals app.\n\n##### Image: About Us 1Leah Hackney\n\nPediatric Dietitian\n\nI’m a board-certified registered dietitian in both the US and Canada. I graduated from California Polytechnic State University in 2014 and completed my dietetic internship at Texas A&M in 2015. I have worked in the pediatric nutrition field for over 10 years working on clinical trials, acute care for NICU/pediatric patients as well as private practice and consulting.\n\nI am passionate about helping families with starting solids, navigating picky eating and generally making meals and feeding kids less stressful.\n\nI am currently the chief of operations for BLW and Kids Meals App where I help run our interdisciplinary feeding team to create research-based and educational content for families to make feeding their babies and kids easier. This includes everything from recipes, feeding guides, meal plans, content on social media platforms, implementing new app features, connecting with other healthcare practitioners and more!\n\nI am the proud mother of two little boys!\n\nMy favorite recipes from BLW Meals and Kids Meals app would probably be the One-Pot Hamburger Helper, Blueberry Lemon Yogurt Muffins and Easy Peasy Pasta.\n\n### Image: About Us 2Christina Garbado\n\nNutritionist and Recipe Developer\n\nI am the proud mom to Tommy and Nico and bring my passion for cooking, good food, and family mealtime to life through my work with our apps. I love helping families make nutritious eating simple and enjoyable.\n\nSince earning my Nutrition degree from Universidade Positivo in Curitiba, Brazil, in 2008, I’ve explored specialties like Children’s Nutrition, Sports Nutrition, and Food Photography. Now, I create and upload recipes for the app, refresh content, and craft posts for Instagram and our website—all to support parents in feeding their kids with confidence. I’m so grateful to share my knowledge and experience with families worldwide. \n\nMy favorite part of my role is testing (and enjoying) the recipes I develop! My all-time favorite is the One-Pot Hamburger Helper—quick, easy, and delicious, just the way family meals should be.\n\n### Image: About Us 3\n\n### Emma Ramker\n\nSpeech Language Pathologist\n\nI am a Speech-Language Pathologist with a Master of Arts in Communication Sciences and Disorders from the University of Central Florida. With experience spanning from babies to geriatrics in various settings, I have spent the last few years of my career focusing on helping families start solids and manage the difficulties of eating during the toddler years.\n\nAs the Content Coordinator for both of our apps and their Instagram accounts, I draw on my expertise as an SLP to ensure all content is accurate, engaging, and impactful.\n\nOutside of work, I’m a proud mom to two—Waverly and Wes. I love making family-friendly favorites from our apps and my go-to recipes are Banana Pancakes, Yogurt Waffles, and Easy Peasy Pasta.\n\n### Image: About Us 4Vanessa Croft\n\nWriter, Educator, and Content Creator\n\nWith over a decade of experience in education and content creation, I am passionate about helping families thrive through engaging, educational, and practical resources. I hold a Master’s degree in English Language from the University of the West Indies (2021) and a Bachelor’s of Education in English Literature (2012), which have equipped me with the skills to create content that empowers parents and caregivers.  \n\nIn my current role, I specialize in developing easy-to-follow content that supports families in building healthy eating habits and navigating mealtime battles. Seeing how our work positively impacts both seasoned and first-time parents is incredibly rewarding. I enjoy being able to use artistic expression to tackle topics that parents may previously only have had access to in parenting books. \n\nAs a mother of three children—Savannah, Harrison, and Scarlett—my personal experiences shape my approach to creating relatable and actionable content. I strive to provide resources that parents can easily integrate into their lives.  My favorite recipe from the apps is the Loaded Veggie Enchilada Casserole which I would gladly eat almost every night of the week. \n\n## Contributors \n\n## Meet the Global Team\n\n### Our App Timeline\n\nImage: Timeline US\n\nImage: Timeline US – Mobile\n\n### Thanks for being here!\n\nWe are incredibly proud to support families worldwide in feeding their children with care and confidence. Our mission is to empower parents and caregivers with the tools, knowledge, and resources they need to provide nutritious, balanced meals during the critical early years. Through our collection of apps, we’ve connected with families from diverse backgrounds, offering guidance on baby-led weaning, food introduction, picky eating and mealtime behavior. Seeing the positive impact on children’s development and the joy families experience when they successfully navigate mealtime challenges reinforces our commitment to creating a more empathetic, supportive approach to child nutrition globally.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBLW Social - Empowering Health & Nutrition for Every Stage of Life (https://app.blwsocial.com/api/promoProxy/8c5a3102-a45c-11e9-8fc5-06e43182e96c/)\nciteturn87search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 9 months ago; \n# BLW Social\n\nBuilding healthier families with science-based nutrition and movement apps — from first bites to active motherhood.\n\nScroll to explore\n\n## Our Apps\n\nDiscover our suite of applications designed to support healthy nutrition at every stage\n\nImage: BLW Brasil Logo\n\n### BLW Brasil\n\nBaby Food Introduction (Brazil)\n\nImage: Garfinho Logo\n\n### Garfinho\n\nChildren's Nutrition for ages 2-7 (Brazil)\n\nImage: BLW Meals Logo\n\n### BLW Meals\n\nBaby Food Introduction (USA)\n\nImage: Kids Meals Logo\n\n### Kids Meals\n\nChildren's Nutrition for ages 2-7 (USA)\n\nImage: BLW Ideas Logo\n\n### BLW Ideas\n\nBaby Food Introduction (Spain)\n\nImage: Peque Ideas Logo\n\n### Peque Ideas\n\nChildren's Nutrition for ages 2-7 (Spain)\n\nImage: Superela Logo\n\n### Superela\n\nNutrition and Exercise for Women\n\n### BLW Social\n\nEmpowering Health & Nutrition for Every Stage of Life\n\nBLW Social is dedicated to providing innovative nutrition solutions for families worldwide. From baby-led weaning to children's meals and women's wellness, we're here to support your health journey.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBLW Meals App | How to Start Solids (https://blwmeals.com/?_branch_match_id=1633836349161271238&_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAAwXBQQqAMAwEwBfZ3gXx4EOkgWhL0yRsCr35dmfqnB57ziRrcJFIxT1J054dNmyjoso4P%2FDDQNP3JtgKxnFV2OAf8RGPFEAAAAA%3D)\nciteturn87search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n# BLW Meals\n\n## How to Start Solids\n\nStart solids confidently to nurture a happy, healthy baby. Your free guide on baby-led weaning and how to offer foods safely, complete with photos and videos.\n\n## Trusted by 4M+ Parents\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nBest starting solids app!\nIslandmom\n“This app is such a helpful tool for parents navigating the early stages of feeding their little ones. The recipes are simple, nutritious, and clearly laid out with preparation tips.”\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nSo helpful\nDahnaRev\n\"The app’s different ways of serving food based on age was super helpful. My daughter is now 2.5 and we constantly get compliments about how well she eats.\"\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nA lifesaver for starting solids!\nEKRmama\n\"This app has saved my life with starting solids, especially with how to handle the top allergy foods. And it’s so much more affordable than some of the other apps!\"\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nSo helpful!\nM57380\n\"I follow BLW on Instagram and the app has been so helpful with recipes and meal plans for each week. ## Some of our features\n\nImage: Home 3\n\n### Free Food Library\n\nWith photos, videos, and tips on how to cut and prepare food safely for your baby whether you offer as finger foods or with responsive spoon-feeding.\n\nImage: Home 4\n\n### 650+ Recipes\n\nMade by pediatric nutritionists and board-certified dietitians (including vegetarian and vegan recipes). Use our filters to find exactly what you’re looking for.\n\nImage: Home 5\n\n### Baby Meals\n\nMonthly meal plans (with a vegetarian option) for all ages (6 months and up), made by board-certified dietitians, along with guidance for allergen introduction.\n\n## See BLW Meals app in action\n\n## Created by\n\nImage: Home 16\n\n### Leah Hackney\n\nPediatric Dietitian\n\nImage: Home 17\n\n### Emma Ramker\n\nSpeech Language Pathologist\n\nImage: Home 18\n\n### Vanessa Croft\n\nContent Creator\n\nImage: Home 19\n\n### Christina Gabardo\n\nRecipe Developer\n\nImage: Home 20\n\n### Dina DiMaggio\n\nPediatrician\n\nImage: Home 21\n\n### Anthony Porto\n\nPediatric Gastroenterologist\n\nImage: Home 22\n\n### Brienna Abraham\n\nFood Therapist and Behavior Analyst\n\nImage: Home 23\n\n### Nicole Lattanzio\n\nPediatric Dietitian & Lactation Consultant\n\n## FAQ\n\nWhat is baby-led weaning?\n\nBaby Led Weaning, often abbreviated as BLW, is a gentle, empowering approach to introducing solid foods to your baby. Instead of being spoon-fed purées, babies following this method are encouraged to feed themselves right from the start using their hands to explore soft, age-appropriate finger foods. The idea is simple but powerful: when babies are developmentally ready (typically around 6 months), they can and should be trusted to feed themselves.\n\nThis approach is rooted in principles of trust, respect, and autonomy. BLW allows babies to decide what, how much, and how quickly they want to eat. It gives them the opportunity to use all their senses during mealtime, supporting the development of fine motor skills, chewing abilities, and even intuitive eating. \nHere in the BLW Meals app, we’re here to support you every step of the way. From expert-approved guides and safe food prep tips to hundreds of nutritionist-created recipes and age-based meal plans, everything you need is at your fingertips. Whether you start with finger foods, purées, or a combination of both, know that there is no perfect way to begin, just the way that works best for you and your baby.\n\nHow can this app help me with BLW?\n\nOne of the first ways the BLW Meals app helps is by showing you exactly when and how to begin. If you’re unsure whether your baby is ready to start solids, there’s a clear and simple checklist to help you identify the signs of readiness like sitting up with support or showing interest in food. Everything in the app is backed by pediatricians and nutritionists, so you know you’re in safe hands.\n\nOnce you’re ready to start, the BLW Meals app becomes your go-to resource for safely offering foods. Inside the Food Library, you’ll find hundreds of foods explained in detail including how to prepare and cut them depending on your baby’s age, whether they’re a common allergen, and how they might affect digestion. You’ll also find guidance on when to start specific foods and tips to make them baby-friendly.\n\nIt’s like having a pediatric nutritionist in your pocket!\n\nThe app also includes over 650 nutritionist-developed recipes made especially for babies. You can search by ingredient, dietary need, age, or texture and even filter out allergens. Whether you’re doing baby-led weaning, spoon-feeding, or a mix of both, you’ll find tons of recipes that fit your style and your baby’s stage.\n\nIf you prefer more structure, the age-based meal plans are a huge help. Each plan is designed by pediatric nutritionists and adjusts as your baby grows. It takes the guesswork out of mealtime, offering inspiration and balance without pressure. You’ll also find expert-reviewed guides on topics that most parents wonder about (like how to tell the difference between gagging and choking, how to introduce allergens safely, and what to do when your baby refuses food). There’s even a guide to help you talk to skeptical family members about baby-led weaning.\n\nAs a bonus, the app helps you stay organized with tools like the Food Tracker, where you can log new foods, note reactions, and keep track of potential allergens.\n\nDoes the information in BLW Meals app get updated regularly?\n\nHere in the BLW Meals app, the content is reviewed and updated regularly by a team of pediatric nutritionists, pediatricians, and speech therapists to make sure everything stays accurate, safe, and in line with the latest recommendations.\n\nWhenever there are meaningful updates like new research, changes in guidelines (especially around allergens or food safety), or feedback from families using the app, the team works behind the scenes to improve or expand the guides, food library entries, and other resources.\n\nYou can feel confident that the information you’re reading isn’t ever outdated, it’s professionally reviewed and always evolving to support you and your baby at every stage of the journey.\n\nAnd if something feels unclear or you’d love to see a new topic added, you can always share feedback by direct messaging us on Instagram or sending us an email. You’re part of this growing, supportive community.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBLW Meals: Starting Solids – Apps bei Google Play (https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?hl=de_AT&id=com.n51951dd8177.app)\nciteturn87search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month; \nDie häufigsten Allergene sind markiert. Einfache Quizfragen in den altersgerechten Ratgebern helfen Ihnen, Ihr Wissen zu überprüfen. Die Ratgeber wachsen mit Ihrem Kind mit.\nWas Eltern über BLW Meals sagen\nIluvpalmtrees ⭐ 5 Sterne\n„Meine Lieblings-BLW-App. So viele kostenlose Informationen